        "summary": "The highest-posterior tree reproduces the paper's K-hub scenario with the two longer chains, and the 24-day median latency. Our single most-likely labelled tree holds a smaller share of the posterior than the paper's reported >99%, because the better-mixing sampler splits probability across trees that differ only in one leaf's parent; grouped by the K-hub scenario the share is far higher.",
